{%- set faqs = [
  ["Why is mobile application security testing important?", "Mobile application security testing helps businesses detect security weaknesses before attackers exploit them. It reduces the risk of data breaches and account compromise while helping protect user privacy and business information."],
  ["What do your mobile app security testing services include?", "Our mobile app security testing services include vulnerability assessments and penetration testing along with authentication checks and API security testing. Depending on the agreed scope, assessments can also cover source code security and data protection practices."],
  ["Do you provide Android and iOS app security testing?", "Yes. We assess both Android and iOS applications to identify platform-specific vulnerabilities and weaknesses in data protection and access controls. Testing scope depends on the application's architecture and the agreed engagement requirements."],
  ["What is the difference between mobile app security testing and penetration testing?", "Mobile app security testing covers a broad range of security checks designed to identify application vulnerabilities. Mobile app penetration testing goes further by attempting to validate how selected vulnerabilities could be exploited through authorized attack simulations."],
  ["How much do mobile app security testing services cost?", "The cost depends on application complexity and the number of platforms along with API coverage and testing depth. Contact our team with your application details to receive a scope-based estimate."],
  ["How long does mobile application security testing take?", "Testing duration depends on application size and functionality along with the number of platforms and identified vulnerabilities. A focused assessment may take a few days while larger applications with extensive API coverage may require several weeks."],
  ["What vulnerabilities can mobile app security testing identify?", "Testing can uncover weak authentication and insecure data storage along with API vulnerabilities and weak encryption practices. It may also identify insecure configurations and vulnerable third-party components that could expose sensitive information."],
  ["Do you provide a report after mobile app security testing?", "Yes. Our deliverables can include an executive summary and a detailed vulnerability report along with severity ratings and remediation recommendations. Retesting and closure documentation can also be included in the agreed scope."],
  ["Do you offer retesting after vulnerabilities are fixed?", "Retesting can be included in the engagement to verify the status of reported vulnerabilities after remediation. The results help development teams confirm that fixes are effective and identify issues that still require attention."],
  ["Which security standards do you follow for mobile application testing?", "We can align relevant testing activities with the OWASP Mobile Application Security Verification Standard (MASVS) and OWASP mobile security testing guidance. The applicable requirements depend on the application type and assessment scope."],
  ["When should a business conduct mobile app security testing?", "Security testing is recommended before a major application release and after significant code changes or new feature integrations. Regular assessments can also help businesses identify emerging vulnerabilities and maintain stronger application security over time."]
] %}

